---
description: Prefer Pond UI primitives over custom-styled controls
alwaysApply: true
---

# Prefer Pond UI

Use `@pond/ui` for interactive controls. Do not hand-roll buttons, menus, dialogs, inputs, or similar chrome with local CSS when a Pond UI primitive exists.

## Do

- `Button` (`variant`, `size`, `icon`) for clicks and icon actions
- `Empty` for empty states
- `Menu`, `Dialog`, `Popover`, `Tooltip`, `TitleBar`, etc. for their jobs
- Local CSS only for layout composition (flex/grid/gap) and one-off product surfaces that are not controls

## Don't

```tsx
// Bad: restyled native control that duplicates Button
<button type="button" className={styles.close} aria-label="Close">
  <IconXmarkOutline18 />
</button>
```

```tsx
// Good: Pond UI owns the control chrome
<Button icon size="xs" variant="ghost" aria-label="Close">
  <IconXmarkOutline18 />
</Button>
```

## Allowed local CSS on Pond UI

- Positioning and flex layout around the control
- Visibility that is product-specific (e.g. show close on tab hover)
- Not colors, radii, paddings, or hover fills that the primitive already defines

If a needed variant is missing from Pond UI, add it there instead of copying the pattern into app CSS.

Do not introduce Tailwind, shadcn, StyleX, raw `@base-ui/react`, or raw `@ui-sdk/*` in app code. Pond UI already wraps Base UI and UI SDK. A behavior Pond UI lacks (reorder, resize, tree, roving focus) gets built in `packages/ui` from UI SDK, then used from the app. Style with CSS Modules. Merge `className` with `import { clsx as cn } from "clsx"`. Do not write a local `cn` helper.
